        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "6 different L shapes.",
          "worked": "The foot is initially 8 cans wide and becomes one can narrower each time. In Diagram 6 it is 3 cans wide, so it still extends beyond the two-can-wide vertical arm. In Diagram 7 it is only 2 cans wide, leaving no projecting foot. Therefore Diagrams 1 to 6 are L shapes.",
